    {
      "title": "What is an Objection",
      "tags": [
        {
          "facet": "topic",
          "label": "objection mindset"
        },
        {
          "facet": "activity",
          "label": "sales training"
        }
      ],
      "span": {
        "start_line": 22,
        "end_line": 37
      },
      "quote": "PART 1 · MINDSET Objection is only a concern that your client has, it's not a rejection of you. 4 It's not the time to react to any objection. You and your client need to work as a team. First to understand the concern, undercover what is behind the concern and then work together as a team to help the client overcome it. 5 PART 1 · MINDSET What's running in your head immediately if the client says: “I will wait and see how the situation with this conflict gonna go.” “It's too expensive.” “I want",
      "item_id": "docs-2026-10-20-session-2-objection-handling-slides-md-1d98819e26:0022-0037",
      "source_id": "docs-2026-10-20-session-2-objection-handling-slides-md-1d98819e26",
      "path": "docs/2026-10-20-Session-2-Objection-Handling-Slides-.md",
      "prev": null,
      "next": "docs-2026-10-20-session-2-objection-handling-slides-md-1d98819e26:0039-0074"
    },
    {
      "title": "Objection Handling Formula",
      "tags": [
        {
          "facet": "topic",
          "label": "objection handling formula"
        },
        {
          "facet": "activity",
          "label": "sales training"
        }
      ],
      "span": {
        "start_line": 39,
        "end_line": 74
      },
      "quote": "PART 2 · THE FORMULA 3-Step Objection Handling Formula 1 Clarify 2 Discuss 3 Diffuse + Agree on the next step where we lead the client Clarify - we never assume, just based on our past experiences, what this means for this exact client. 7 STEP 1 · CLARIFY Clarifying Questions to Ask “Now…when you say (repeat back what they said) what do you mean by that?” “I'm curious, did you ask me that for a reason?” “Can I ask where you got this information from?” 8 STEP 1 · CLARIFY Clarifying Questions to A",
      "item_id": "docs-2026-10-20-session-2-objection-handling-slides-md-1d98819e26:0039-0074",
      "source_id": "docs-2026-10-20-session-2-objection-handling-slides-md-1d98819e26",
      "path": "docs/2026-10-20-Session-2-Objection-Handling-Slides-.md",
      "prev": "docs-2026-10-20-session-2-objection-handling-slides-md-1d98819e26:0022-0037",
      "next": "docs-2026-10-20-session-2-objection-handling-slides-md-1d98819e26:0339-0422"
    },
    {
      "title": "Objection Handling Exercise",
      "tags": [
        {
          "facet": "topic",
          "label": "objection handling practice"
        },
        {
          "facet": "activity",
          "label": "roleplay exercise"
        }
      ],
      "span": {
        "start_line": 339,
        "end_line": 422
      },
      "quote": "PRACTICE Two Teams. One List. Team A Gives the client an objection from the list — call out the number. Team B The agent handles it: Clarify → Discuss → Diffuse → Agree on the next step. Observer Checks the agent and gives feedback. Switch teams after every round. 47 PART 2 · THE FORMULA 3-Step Objection Handling Formula 1 Clarify 2 Discuss 3 Diffuse + Agree on the next step where we lead the client Clarify - we never assume, just based on our past experiences, what this means for this exact cli",
      "item_id": "docs-2026-10-20-session-2-objection-handling-slides-md-1d98819e26:0339-0422",
      "source_id": "docs-2026-10-20-session-2-objection-handling-slides-md-1d98819e26",
      "path": "docs/2026-10-20-Session-2-Objection-Handling-Slides-.md",
      "prev": "docs-2026-10-20-session-2-objection-handling-slides-md-1d98819e26:0039-0074",
      "next": null
    },
    {
      "title": "Clarify",
      "tags": [
        {
          "facet": "topic",
          "label": "clarifying objections"
        },
        {
          "facet": "activity",
          "label": "sales coaching"
        }
      ],
      "span": {
        "start_line": 28,
        "end_line": 35
      },
      "quote": "1. Clarify → 2. Discuss → 3. Diffuse Clarify - we never assume, just based on our past experiences, what this means for this exact client. Clarifying Questions to Ask * “Now…when you say (repeat back what they said) what do you mean by that?” * “I'm curious, did you ask me that for a reason?” * “Can I ask where you got this information from?” * “Can you tell me more about that?” * “When you say (repeat back the concern), what's behind that, just so I understand?”",
      "item_id": "docs-2026-10-20-session-2-objection-handling-workbook-md-a41b963961:0028-0035",
      "source_id": "docs-2026-10-20-session-2-objection-handling-workbook-md-a41b963961",
      "path": "docs/2026-10-20-Session-2-Objection-Handling-Workbook-.md",
      "prev": null,
      "next": "docs-2026-10-20-session-2-objection-handling-workbook-md-a41b963961:0036-0036"
    },
    {
      "title": "Discuss",
      "tags": [
        {
          "facet": "topic",
          "label": "discussing objections"
        },
        {
          "facet": "activity",
          "label": "sales coaching"
        }
      ],
      "span": {
        "start_line": 36,
        "end_line": 36
      },
      "quote": "Discuss - When you understand what is the actual concern you can discuss what are the possible ways to overcome it.",
      "item_id": "docs-2026-10-20-session-2-objection-handling-workbook-md-a41b963961:0036-0036",
      "source_id": "docs-2026-10-20-session-2-objection-handling-workbook-md-a41b963961",
      "path": "docs/2026-10-20-Session-2-Objection-Handling-Workbook-.md",
      "prev": "docs-2026-10-20-session-2-objection-handling-workbook-md-a41b963961:0028-0035",
      "next": "docs-2026-10-20-session-2-objection-handling-workbook-md-a41b963961:0037-0047"
    },
    {
      "title": "Diffuse",
      "tags": [
        {
          "facet": "topic",
          "label": "diffusing objections"
        },
        {
          "facet": "activity",
          "label": "sales coaching"
        }
      ],
      "span": {
        "start_line": 37,
        "end_line": 47
      },
      "quote": "Diffuse - Offer a perspective, or a solution, that did work for other clients before. * “Can I offer a suggestion? The way the other clients did that is…” * “Do you feel this could be an option for you?” Your Turn Pick the clarifying question you will use most. Write it out word for word, until you can say it without thinking. ______________________________________________________________________ ______________________________________________________________________ Which step do you usually ski",
